 * {@code MALFORMED} results for the same input characters.  The new
 * implementation guarantees forward progress by:
 *
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Setting the encoder to {@code REPORT} mode for malformed and
 *       unmappable input, so that we can handle those cases explicitly.</li>
 *   <li>Replacing erroneous input with the encoder's replacement byte
 *       sequence and advancing the {@link CharBuffer}'s position.</li>
 *   <li>Growing the output {@link ByteBuffer} whenever an overflow occurs.</li>
 *   <li>Ensuring that each loop iteration either consumes at least one
 *       character or expands the buffer, preventing an endless loop.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * The method now works correctly for all execution paths and is safe for
 * production use under Java 7.
 */
